  "enhanced_information": "The Gram stain differentiates bacteria based on the different composition of the cell wall of Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. It involves crystal violet and safranin, where Gram-positive bacteria retain the crystal violet dye due to their thicker peptidoglycan layer, while Gram-negative bacteria are counterstained pink by safranin. This staining process is observed under a microscope."
